// The PopupApp target uses `SupabaseProject.xcconfig` (tracked) for SUPABASE_URL.
//
// xcconfig quirk: a bare `https://...` is parsed as `https:` because `//` starts a comment.
// In SupabaseProject.xcconfig the URL uses: https:/$()/YOUR_REF.supabase.co
//
// Optional override in Secrets.xcconfig:
//   SUPABASE_AUTH_REDIRECT_URL = https:/$()/your.domain/auth/verified.html
//
// Create `Secrets.xcconfig` in this folder (gitignored) with:
//   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = eyJ...your_anon_key...
//   SQUARE_APPLICATION_ID = sandbox-sq0idb-...        (sq0idp-... for production)
//   APPLE_PAY_MERCHANT_ID = merchant.com.popup.app
//
// TestFlight / App Store (Release) builds, also in Secrets.xcconfig or SupabaseProject.xcconfig:
//   API_BASE_URL_RELEASE = https:/$()/your-backend.example.com/api
//   POPUP_RELEASE_ENTITLEMENTS = PopupApp.ApplePay.entitlements
//     PopupApp.entitlements          -> no payment entitlements (default, always archives)
//     PopupApp.ApplePay.entitlements -> Apple Pay; requires the Merchant ID above to exist in the portal
//     PopupApp.Payments.entitlements -> Apple Pay + Tap to Pay; requires Apple's approval of the
//                                        Tap to Pay on iPhone entitlement for your team
//
// Notes:
// - Square application ID goes in iOS Secrets.xcconfig; access token and secret stay in backend/.env
// - Debug builds default API_BASE_URL to http://127.0.0.1:5001/api (match backend PORT)
// - Release builds have no localhost fallback and require an HTTPS API_BASE_URL_RELEASE
// - Tap to Pay needs an Organization team and a physical iPhone XS+.
//
// SupabaseProject.xcconfig includes Secrets.xcconfig when present.
